  "offensiveAbilities": [
    {
      "name": "Boat Breaker",
      "actions": null,
      "traits": [],
      "description": "<p>A kongamato's beak is supernaturally hard. Their beak Strikes ignore half the Hardness of any object they hit.</p>",
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "name": "Flying Strafe",
      "actions": 2,
      "traits": [],
      "description": "<p>The kongamato Flies up to their fly Speed and makes two wing Strikes at any point during that movement. Each Strike must target a different creature.</p>",
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "name": "Wailing Dive",
      "actions": 2,
      "traits": [],
      "description": "<p>The kongamato Flies while emitting a terrifying screech. Each creature the kongamato flies over must succeed at a DC 30 Will Saving Throw save or become Frightened 1 (Frightened 2 on a critical failure).</p>\n<p>After attempting their saves, the creatures are temporarily immune for 1 hour. At the end of their movement, the kongamato can make a beak Strike.</p>",
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "name": "Grab",
      "actions": 1,
      "traits": [],
      "description": "<p><details><summary>See rules...</summary>\n<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p></details></p>",
      "collapsed": false
    }
  ],
